r others above everything, excellent attention skills. Decision quality good, attention good, but communication issues, egocentric, not willing to develop.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as loner. Good problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to start discussion, maybe propose candidate B as leading due to strong reliability and stress handling, despite communication tone issues. Or candidate D? Let's pick B as initial recommendation.\n\nWe need to reference facts: B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), but pretentious and wrong tone (communication). Argue that strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nProvide vote B.\n\nProceed."}
